Look over the saxpy.c code.

1.) The following saxpy.c code uses the same variant method shown in dev_or_host_variant.c.
    Moreover it requires mapping data to the device.  In many cases, storage is often
    made persistent though out many GPU offloads. The target_data in main()
    makes x and y data persistent throughout target_data region (block), by
    mapping array sections of the x and y pointers.

2.) Note, the use_device_ptr(x,y) cause instructs the d_saxpy() function to
    use the device pointers in the arguments.
